There are no result rows. Neither 1 nor NULL produces true, and 2 is a known blocked value.

after:
Run this example in a fresh database:
```sql
CREATE TABLE candidates(id INTEGER);
CREATE TABLE blocked(id INTEGER);
INSERT INTO candidates VALUES (1), (2), (NULL);
INSERT INTO blocked VALUES (2), (NULL);
SELECT c.id
FROM candidates AS c
WHERE c.id IS NOT NULL
  AND NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM blocked AS b WHERE b.id = c.id
  )
ORDER BY c.id;
```
Only `1` is returned. ID 2 is blocked, and the missing candidate is excluded explicitly.
